(footprint "BN61-2402_Vertical_HandWound_SecondaryCT"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "manual")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Fair-Rite BN61-2402 small binocular ferrite core (type 61 material, 7.52 x 7.52 x 5.08 mm per Fair-Rite 2861002402 datasheet; two 1.52 mm dia bores on 2.54 mm pitch). Mounted VERTICALLY (standing on end). Hand-wound, 5-pad layout for a transformer where the SECONDARY winding has a center tap and the primary does not. Pad layout: pins 1 and 2 are the two ends of the 2-pin non-tapped winding (primary); pins 3, 4, 5 are the two ends and center-tap of the 3-pin tapped winding (secondary, with pin 4 as the CT). Used in Rev D for T201 input transformer on ss_pa: pins 1,2 = single-ended RF input primary (1 = RF in, 2 = GND); pins 3,4,5 = bifilar secondary driving BS170 PP gates (3,5 = gate A, gate B; 4 = CT where DRIVER_BIAS DAC injects DC bias). Companion to BN61-2402_Vertical_HandWound_PrimaryCT -- physically identical, pad numbers swapped for symbol compatibility. VERIFY body dimensions against actual stock before fab.")
	(tags "ferrite binocular bn61-2402 fair-rite type-61 vertical hand-wound transformer center-tap secondary")
